VI. DENSITIES OF STATES
The densities of states as a function of energy were investigated for the isolated molecule and the most likely model M1 and are reported in Figs. 7(a) and 7(b). In order to assist our interpretation of the HOMO and LUMO states, the corresponding local densities of states were also calculated (Fig. 8). Concerning the isolated molecule, they were compared to the results of Chi ̧s et al.28 and good agreement was obtained for both the HOMO and the LUMO. Let us first consider the HOMO. Comparing the LDOS of the isolated molecule to those of the chemisorbed molecule, we observe a small deformation of the HOMO on the surface. The overall symmetry of the molecular orbital with respect to the long axis
